larmorx-freesurfer holds bit-exact replicas of FreeSurfer's programs: Rust translations of
FreeSurfer 8.2.0's source code, written to give its output bit for bit. They are modified versions
of FreeSurfer, marked as such here and in every translated file (each names its origin in a
comment and its licence in an SPDX header, LicenseRef-FreeSurfer; each crate's PROVENANCE.md lists
the FreeSurfer files it was translated from and the changes made), and they are distributed under
the FreeSurfer Software License (LICENSE: its Part B, prefaced with the words its paragraph 1(b)
requires; the complete agreement as FreeSurfer 8.2.0 ships it is LICENSES/FreeSurfer-LICENSE.txt).
Every user receives those terms: among them, the software is designed for research purposes only
and has not been reviewed or approved by the Food and Drug Administration or any other agency;
clinical applications are neither recommended nor advised (paragraph 4); it is provided "AS IS",
without warranty, and every user assumes the liability for its use (paragraph 5). Its source code
is published at https://github.com/karellopez/larmorx (directory crates-freesurfer/).

The program is a separate work from larmorx (Apache-2.0), which runs it as a separate process
when it is installed and exchanges files with it only. It is not the original FreeSurfer, does not
present itself as FreeSurfer, and is not endorsed by The General Hospital Corporation, the
Athinoula A. Martinos Center for Biomedical Imaging or FreeSurfer's developers (paragraph 6).
FreeSurfer's own programs ask for a licence key (license.txt); that is a check inside FreeSurfer's
programs, not a term of its licence, and larmorx-freesurfer asks for none (docs/licensing.md).


Translated works
================

FreeSurfer 8.2.0 (https://github.com/freesurfer/freesurfer, tag v8.2.0), Copyright © 2021 The
General Hospital Corporation (Boston, MA) "MGH" (as its files carry it; a few say 2011) - the
FreeSurfer Software License, version 1.0 (LICENSE)
  FreeSurfer's files say: "Terms and conditions for use, reproduction, distribution and
  contribution are found in the 'FreeSurfer Software License Agreement' contained in the file
  'LICENSE' found in the FreeSurfer distribution". The authors each file names are kept in the
  translated files' comments.
  Translated: none yet (queue item 3.1-01 created the workspace: the program, the wheel and empty
  crates; docs/freesurfer/queue.md lists what comes next).
  Modified: translated from C and C++ to Rust in 2026 by Karel Lopez Vilaret; the defects of
  FreeSurfer's that change results are corrected by default and reproduced on request
  (LARMORX_UPSTREAM_DEFECTS=reproduce; the FS entries of the repository's
  docs/findings/upstream-defects.md); the maths default to correctly rounded functions.
  The licence grants rights only in MGH's own software (paragraph 3): the third-party code
  inside FreeSurfer is translated from its own upstream under its own licence (below, as each is
  added), or replaced by larmorx's own code, as docs/freesurfer/third-party.md places it.


